        <div class="faq-list" data-faq>
          <!-- faq:start -->
          <div class="faq-item is-open">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-a1"><span>Who is MAD Funnel Design for?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q1"><div><p>MAD Funnel Design is for coaches, consultants, creators and service-based businesses that need a website, landing page or sales funnel built around their offer. Aldrich Matthew designs and develops each project himself, from the page structure and visual design to the forms and automation behind it.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a2"><span>How much does a website or sales funnel cost?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q2"><div><p>Packages start at $850 USD for a single custom landing page. A multi-page website or defined sales funnel starts at $2,200, and a custom multi-page system for established businesses starts at $4,500. These are starting estimates; the final quote depends on scope and complexity. See the <a href="#pricing">full package breakdown</a>.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a3"><span>What is included in the $850 Web Essentials package?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q3"><div><p>Web Essentials covers one custom landing page with a conversion-focused structure, custom visual design, responsive desktop and mobile layouts, lead capture forms with basic integrations, basic on-page SEO setup, testing and deployment. Advanced GSAP and Lenis animation is available separately.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a4"><span>What is the difference between a landing page and a sales funnel?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q4"><div><p>A landing page is a single page built to get one action, such as a booking or an enquiry. A sales funnel is a connected sequence of pages and follow-up steps that guides a visitor from first interest to a sale or booked call. Which one fits depends on your offer and sales process.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a5"><span>Do you build with Systeme.io, GoHighLevel or custom code?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q5"><div><p>All three. Projects are built with custom HTML, CSS and JavaScript, or on platforms such as Systeme.io, GoHighLevel and Shopify when the project calls for them. The choice depends on what you need to manage yourself, how your leads are handled, and how much control the design requires.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a6"><span>Can you connect my website to a CRM and automate follow-ups?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q6"><div><p>Yes. Lead capture forms can be connected to your CRM, with automated follow-up emails, pipeline stages and customer workflows set up behind them. Web &amp; Conversion includes CRM integration and up to 2 automation workflows; Web Systems covers advanced CRM integrations and multi-step workflows.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a7"><span>Is SEO included in my website?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q7"><div><p>Yes, at a level that depends on the package. Web Essentials includes basic on-page SEO setup, Web &amp; Conversion includes on-page SEO foundations, and Web Systems adds technical SEO. SEO supports how your site is found and understood, but no specific ranking or traffic result is guaranteed.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a8"><span>How does a project work from brief to launch?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a8" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q8"><div><p>Every project follows four steps: understanding your requirements, planning the structure and design, developing and connecting the site, then testing and launching it. You see the direction before development begins, and mobile, desktop, links, forms and integrations are checked before launch. Read the <a href="#process">full process</a>.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a9"><span>How long does a project take, and are revisions included?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a9" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q9"><div><p>Timelines and revision allowances depend on the scope, so they are set out in your written proposal before work starts. A single landing page and a multi-page system with automation are very different projects, which is why a fixed number would not be accurate for everyone.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q10" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a10"><span>Are hosting, domains and subscriptions included in the price?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a10" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q10"><div><p>No, unless your proposal says otherwise. Hosting, domain names, third-party subscriptions and paid integrations are billed separately by their providers. Prices cover the design, development, setup and deployment work.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q11" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a11"><span>Do you guarantee leads, sales or search rankings?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a11" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q11"><div><p>No. A well-structured website and funnel makes it easier for visitors to understand your offer and take the next step, but results also depend on your offer, traffic, pricing and market. No lead, revenue, conversion or ranking outcome is guaranteed.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3><button class="faq-q" type="button" id="faq-q12" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a12"><span>Do you work with clients outside the Philippines?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
            <div class="faq-a" id="faq-a12" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q12"><div><p>Yes. Aldrich is based in the Philippines and works with coaches and service-based businesses worldwide. Pricing is in USD, and projects are handled online. The easiest way to start is to <a href="https://calendly.com/-aldrichmatthew/15mins">book a free 15-minute call</a>.</p></div></div>
